  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Judges",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 10,
    "summary": "Tola and then Jair judge Israel—The children of Israel worship false gods, are forsaken by the Lord, and are distressed by their enemies—They repent and ask the Lord for deliverance.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And after Abimelech there arose to defend Israel Tola the son of Puah, the son of Dodo, a man of Issachar; and he dwelt in Shamir in mount Ephraim.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "HEB deliver, save."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 10:1",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And he judged Israel twenty and three years, and died, and was buried in Shamir.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 10:2",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And after him arose Jair, a Gileadite, and judged Israel twenty and two years.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 10:3",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And he had thirty sons that rode on thirty ass colts, and they had thirty cities, which are called Havoth-jair unto this day, which are in the land of Gilead.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 132,
            "end": 135
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 10:4",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And Jair died, and was buried in Camon.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 10:5",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And the children of Israel did evil again in the sight of the Lord, and served Baalim, and Ashtaroth, and the gods of Syria, and the gods of Zidon, and the gods of Moab, and the gods of the children of Ammon, and the gods of the Philistines, and forsook the Lord, and served not him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 10:6",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And the anger of the Lord was hot against Israel, and he sold them into the hands of the Philistines, and into the hands of the children of Ammon.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 61,
            "text": "Hel. 12:3 (2–6)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 10:7",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And that year they vexed and oppressed the children of Israel: eighteen years, all the children of Israel that were on the other side Jordan in the land of the Amorites, which is in Gilead.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 111,
            "end": 115
          },
          {
            "start": 176,
            "end": 178
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 10:8",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Moreover the children of Ammon passed over Jordan to fight also against Judah, and against Benjamin, and against the house of Ephraim; so that Israel was sore distressed.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 10:9",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And the children of Israel cried unto the Lord, saying, We have sinned against thee, both because we have forsaken our God, and also served Baalim.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "1 Sam. 7:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
